  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Studios, Inc. (Petitioners)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Studios, Inc. (Petitioners), according to Metro\u2011Goldwyn\u2011Mayer Studios, Inc. (Petitioners), copyright infringement is the only commercially significant use of the Grokster and StreamCast services, indicating a business model built on infringement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Clement, the lower court allowed companies to build a business model out of copyright infringement without fear of secondary liability."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Clement, a study by petitioners\u2019 experts shows how the system operates to facilitate infringement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Clement, the Ninth Circuit got the analysis wrong by relying on a combination of public\u2011domain works and anecdotal evidence of authorized sharing."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Clement, under the Sony test, a clear business model that targets infringing uses should satisfy the inducement standard before reaching actual inducement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Taranto",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Taranto, because the software products have large and growing legitimate uses, their distribution is protected under the Sony rule."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, all past acts constitute a basis for inducement liability, which the Court could affirm."
        }
      ],
